#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: /./,/^$/!d
# 25. Squeeze runs of blank lines to one, like cat -s. Pement: sed '/./,/^$/!d'
# The range runs from a non-blank line to the next blank line, inclusive;
# !d deletes everything outside it, which is the second and later blank
# lines of every run, and blank lines at the top of the file. To delete all
# blank lines the sheet has  sed '/^$/d' ; leading ones only,  sed '/./,$!d'.
# Try: /^$/d  and the two groups of states run together.
/./,/^$/!d

#DATA


Alabama
Alaska



Iowa


Ohio
